From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rzg2l-smarc-som: add ramoops reserved-memory
 region

Reserve 256 KB at the top of RAM (0xBFFC0000) for the kernel's
pstore_ram backend. U-Boot doesn't zero RAM on warm reset, so the
contents survive into the next boot under /sys/fs/pstore/ where
operations can read the last oops/panic + console + pmsg.

Layout inside the 256 KB:
  - 4 x 16 KB kmsg records (panic/oops dumps)
  - 64 KB console buffer
  - 64 KB userspace pmsg buffer
  - 16 byte ECC per region

`no-map` prevents the kernel's page allocator from touching the area,
which would otherwise clobber the contents shortly after boot.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific configuration]
Signed-off-by: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/rzg2l-smarc-som.dtsi | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/rzg2l-smarc-som.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/rzg2l-smarc-som.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/rzg2l-smarc-som.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/rzg2l-smarc-som.dtsi
@@ -55,6 +55,15 @@
 			reg = <0x0 0x68000000 0x0 0x8000000>;
 		};

+		ramoops@bffc0000 {
+			compatible = "ramoops";
+			reg = <0x0 0xbffc0000 0x0 0x40000>;
+			record-size = <0x4000>;
+			console-size = <0x10000>;
+			pmsg-size = <0x10000>;
+			ecc-size = <16>;
+			no-map;
+		};
 	};

 	mmngr {
--
